
=== the wait and the token are what the peer is asked for
the request says how long the peer may hold it: ok
and what this client last had: ok

=== a peer that says it understood is taken at its word
the answer is passed straight up, having been waited for: ok
a client that has nothing to compare sends no token: ok

=== a peer too old to know the parameter is paced from this end
an answer that cost no time is floored before returning: ok
